@startuml sighup-reload
title logfence — SIGHUP Hot Reload Sequence

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA

actor "Operator" as Ops
participant "Signal Handler\n(main.rs)" as Signals
participant "Config Loader\n(config.rs)" as Config
participant "Validator Builder\n(main.rs)" as Builder
participant "watch::Sender\n(main.rs)" as Sender
participant "Session A\n(active)" as SessionA
participant "Session B\n(active)" as SessionB

note over SessionA, SessionB
  Both sessions are mid-stream,
  processing messages concurrently.
  Each holds a watch::Receiver clone.
end note

Ops -> Signals : kill -HUP <pid>

Signals -> Config : load config file from disk
Config --> Signals : Config { validation: ... }

Signals -> Builder : load_schema_files(cfg.validation)
Builder -> Builder : read JSON schema files\ncompile with jsonschema
Builder --> Signals : Vec<JsonSchemaValidator>

Signals -> Builder : build_validator(cfg.validation, schemas)
Builder --> Signals : Arc<Validator> (new)

Signals -> Sender : validator_tx.send(Arc<new_validator>)
note right of Sender
  watch channel update is
  atomic and lock-free.
  No connections dropped.
end note

note over SessionA, SessionB
  Sessions continue processing
  in-flight messages with the
  old validator until the next
  message boundary.
end note

SessionA -> SessionA : finish current message\nwith old Validator

SessionA -> Sender : borrow() — picks up\nnew Arc<Validator>
note right of SessionA
  Clone Arc from borrow(),
  release borrow lock before
  any await point.
end note
SessionA -> SessionA : process next message\nwith new Validator

SessionB -> SessionB : finish current message\nwith old Validator
SessionB -> Sender : borrow() — picks up\nnew Arc<Validator>
SessionB -> SessionB : process next message\nwith new Validator

note over SessionA, SessionB
  Zero downtime:
  - No connections dropped
  - No messages lost
  - New schema takes effect
    at next message boundary
  - Old Arc dropped when
    last session releases it
end note

@enduml
